# 20. PROFIT CALCULATION

Profit should be calculated correctly.

For each sold unit:

Profit:

Selling price - Purchase cost

For multiple units:

Profit:

(Selling price per unit - Purchase cost per unit) × quantity sold

For installment sales, distinguish between:

### Sales revenue

Total selling value of the sale.

### Money collected

Actual amount customers have paid so far.

### Outstanding balance

Total selling value - money collected.

Do not incorrectly classify unpaid installment balances as money already collected.

Clearly label these metrics.

